# Scoped to this directory only.
#
# The wideners are applied with `git apply', which needs the patch body to match
# its target byte for byte -- a CRLF checkout makes every hunk fail.  The shell
# drivers run on Linux, where a CRLF line ending produces the classic
# "\r: command not found".  Both are silent-ish failures that look like a broken
# test rather than a broken checkout, so pin the endings here.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.lisp  text eol=lf
